// A collection's accessors are declared without a parameter list, so a call with `()` is an error
// naming the fix, on a representative of each family: a vector, a list, a range, a set, a map.
// error: `head` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `head`, not `head()`
// error: `tail` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `tail`, not `tail()`
// error: `isEmpty` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `isEmpty`, not `isEmpty()`
// error: `size` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `size`, not `size()`
// error: `keys` takes no parameter list, so it is called without parentheses: write `keys`, not `keys()`

main()
  println([1, 2].head())
  println(List(1, 2).tail())
  println((1 ..< 3).isEmpty())
  println(HashSet.from([1]).size())
  println(Map((1, "a")).keys())
